1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,546
Hi, this is Tanmay Kulkarni,
in for Humanitarians AI.

2
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:06,574
This receipt came out of an
early version of my own build.

3
00:00:06,614 --> 00:00:12,041
An AI agent bought $42.50 of groceries,
and the receipt says Morgan approved it.

4
00:00:12,416 --> 00:00:13,592
Morgan never saw it.

5
00:00:14,383 --> 00:00:16,324
So now I read receipts backwards.

6
00:00:16,449 --> 00:00:19,586
Start at the bottom, and for
every line, ask one question.

7
00:00:19,626 --> 00:00:22,685
Which step checked this,
before it was written down?

8
00:00:22,891 --> 00:00:25,784
The agent line was checked:
registered, and verified.

9
00:00:25,824 --> 00:00:28,143
In that early version,
the person line wasn't.

10
00:00:28,183 --> 00:00:31,977
Nothing compared who the agent belongs
to with who it said it was buying for.

11
00:00:32,017 --> 00:00:34,151
Now one step does,
and Devon's agent buying

12
00:00:34,171 --> 00:00:37,113
"for Morgan" is stopped
before anything else runs.

13
00:00:37,775 --> 00:00:40,906
Then, while making this video,
I found another line like that.

14
00:00:40,946 --> 00:00:44,063
Devon's rule covered groceries
until the end of 2026.

15
00:00:44,167 --> 00:00:46,679
An order dated after that
should come back to Devon.

16
00:00:46,719 --> 00:00:49,786
Spell the category with a capital H,
and the lookup missed the rule,

17
00:00:49,826 --> 00:00:52,208
the demo's gate said yes,
and it went through.

18
00:00:52,248 --> 00:00:55,012
Now every category is
compared in one spelling.

19
00:00:55,616 --> 00:00:57,818
Both of those receipts looked perfect.

20
00:00:57,858 --> 00:01:00,336
Mastercard describes its
record as tamper-resistant,

21
00:01:00,356 --> 00:01:03,610
and a seal like that can show
nobody changed the record.

22
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:05,308
It can't make the lines true.

23
00:01:05,348 --> 00:01:09,876
That part comes from the checks before it,
like the ones on the rest of this receipt.

24
00:01:09,916 --> 00:01:13,096
Which leaves one line on mine.
Merchant. It's carried, not checked,

25
00:01:13,116 --> 00:01:15,836
because Mastercard hasn't
published how that check works.

26
00:01:15,856 --> 00:01:18,132
So the build says so, instead of guessing.

27
00:01:18,172 --> 00:01:20,651
Every line is either earned,
or honestly marked.

28
00:01:20,691 --> 00:01:24,338
The full video reads the whole
receipt, and it's linked below.
